  <p class="sub" style="margin-top:18px">Everything runs client-side — your data never leaves the tab. Bookmark once; no extension can be yanked from under you again. <a href="index.html">All 90+ tools →</a></p>
  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <details><summary>Why did my utility extension disappear?</summary><p>Chrome completed the Manifest V2 phase-out in 2025–2026: MV2 extensions were disabled, then removed from the Web Store. Utility extensions (JSON viewers, pickers, text tools) that were never ported died with it. Security extensions needing <code>webRequest</code> (e.g. classic uBlock Origin) can't be replaced by a webpage — but every read-only utility can.</p></details>
  <details><summary>Do these tools send my data anywhere?</summary><p>No. Every tool on this site is 100% client-side JavaScript — paste stays in the tab, nothing is uploaded, no account, no tracking.</p></details>
  <details><summary>Will these disappear like extensions did?</summary><p>They can't be remotely disabled — they're plain pages. The whole site is open source on <a href="https://github.com/zalize-com/trendscope">GitHub</a>; you can even self-host it.</p></details>
